<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
    §9.4.3's severity shapes, as path geometry.

    These are tokens rather than part of any one control's template, and they moved here from
    Themes/Generic.xaml when a second consumer appeared (#32). Generic.xaml is the control-library
    default-styles dictionary: WinUI loads it for custom control templates, but it is NOT merged
    into Application.Resources, so a page referencing a key defined only there resolves nothing at
    run time. A control template still finds these, because ThemeResource lookup walks up to the
    application.

    Each path is drawn in a 12x12 box so the five are optically consistent, and the distinctions
    are deliberately coarse - filled circle, triangle, hexagon, circled i, hollow ring - because
    they have to survive being small, being greyscale, and being seen from across a room. That is
    also what makes them the second channel A11Y-12 requires: colour convergence under protanopia
    or deuteranopia does not touch a shape, and neither does high contrast collapsing every
    severity brush onto SystemColorWindowTextColor.
-->
<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <x:String x:Key="WzShapeCircle">M 0,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 12,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 0,6 Z</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="WzShapeTriangle">M 6,0 L 12,11 L 0,11 Z</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="WzShapeHexagon">M 6,0 L 11.2,3 L 11.2,9 L 6,12 L 0.8,9 L 0.8,3 Z</x:String>
    <!-- F0 is the even-odd fill rule, which is what knocks the glyph out of the disc. -->
    <x:String x:Key="WzShapeInfo">F0 M 0,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 12,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 0,6 Z M 5.1,5.1 L 6.9,5.1 L 6.9,9.4 L 5.1,9.4 Z M 5.1,2.4 L 6.9,2.4 L 6.9,4.1 L 5.1,4.1 Z</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="WzShapeRing">F0 M 0,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 12,6 A 6,6 0 1 0 0,6 Z M 2.4,6 A 3.6,3.6 0 1 0 9.6,6 A 3.6,3.6 0 1 0 2.4,6 Z</x:String>

    <!--
        §9.9's four custom icons, authored 30 Aug 2026 (#320). None of them existed; the Satellites
        and Holdover nav items borrowed stock Globe and Pause, the medallion borrowed a generic
        Warning for a specific state, and no sky-plot or oscillator glyph was drawn anywhere.

        DRAWN AS FILLED GEOMETRY, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME THING AS §9.9'S "1.5 px stroke".
        PathIcon FILLS its Data with Foreground and cannot stroke it, so every stroke here is
        authored as a 1.5-wide filled band - a ring is an outer circle with an inner one knocked out
        by the even-odd rule, and a bar whose width equals twice its corner radius is a stadium. The
        weight §9.9 asks for is preserved; only the means differ, and the means are forced by the
        control. The alternative - a Path with Stroke inside a Viewbox - is not an IconElement and so
        cannot be a NavigationViewItem's Icon, which is where three of the four are needed.

        16x16 with a 1 px safe margin, per §9.9. Terminals and joins are rounded at 0.75. Monochrome,
        because the Foreground they inherit is what makes them recolour under theme and high
        contrast. Optically rather than mathematically centred: the two circular glyphs run to 6.5
        where a square one stops at 6, which is §9.9's ~2% correction.

        Provisional as drawings. Tony asked for simple icons to tune later (#320), so these are built
        to be legible at 16 and easy to replace rather than finished artwork; the wiring around them
        is the part that is meant to last.
    -->

    <!--
        Satellite: two panels, a body, and the arms between them.

        Each panel is TWO bars rather than one solid block, which is both the cell division a real
        array has and the thing that brought this icon back to the stock glyphs' weight. Drawn solid
        first and measured against the Fluent items above and below it in the pane, where it read as
        a second, heavier set - exactly what §9.9's optical-weight rule exists to prevent. Outlining
        the panels instead was not available: at 16 px a 3.5-wide panel with a 1.5 wall leaves a
        0.5 hole, which fills in at any scaling that is not exactly 100%.
    -->
    <x:String x:Key="WzIconSatellite">M 2.25,5.75 H 4.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 5,6.5 V 6.875 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 4.25,7.625 H 2.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 1.5,6.875 V 6.5 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 2.25,5.75 Z M 2.25,8.375 H 4.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 5,9.125 V 9.5 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 4.25,10.25 H 2.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 1.5,9.5 V 9.125 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 2.25,8.375 Z M 11.75,5.75 H 13.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 14.5,6.5 V 6.875 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 13.75,7.625 H 11.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 11,6.875 V 6.5 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 11.75,5.75 Z M 11.75,8.375 H 13.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 14.5,9.125 V 9.5 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 13.75,10.25 H 11.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 11,9.5 V 9.125 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 11.75,8.375 Z M 7.25,6.5 H 8.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 9.5,7.25 V 8.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 8.75,9.5 H 7.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 6.5,8.75 V 7.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 7.25,6.5 Z M 5,7.25 H 6.5 V 8.75 H 5 Z M 9.5,7.25 H 11 V 8.75 H 9.5 Z</x:String>

    <!--
        Sky plot: the polar grid itself - an azimuth ring, an elevation ring, and the zenith at the
        centre. Two rings and a dot, which is the drawing SkyPlotControl actually makes.
    -->
    <x:String x:Key="WzIconSkyPlot">F0 M 1.5,8 A 6.5,6.5 0 1 0 14.5,8 A 6.5,6.5 0 1 0 1.5,8 Z M 3,8 A 5,5 0 1 0 13,8 A 5,5 0 1 0 3,8 Z M 4.75,8 A 3.25,3.25 0 1 0 11.25,8 A 3.25,3.25 0 1 0 4.75,8 Z M 6.25,8 A 1.75,1.75 0 1 0 9.75,8 A 1.75,1.75 0 1 0 6.25,8 Z M 7,8 A 1,1 0 1 0 9,8 A 1,1 0 1 0 7,8 Z</x:String>

    <!--
        Oscillator: §9.9 names the form exactly - a sine in a rounded square. The wave is two
        half-period bands rather than one path, because a band that crosses its own inflection cannot
        be written as a single offset arc pair; at 16 px the join is invisible and the shape reads.
    -->
    <x:String x:Key="WzIconOscillator">F0 M 4.5,1.5 H 11.5 A 3,3 0 0 1 14.5,4.5 V 11.5 A 3,3 0 0 1 11.5,14.5 H 4.5 A 3,3 0 0 1 1.5,11.5 V 4.5 A 3,3 0 0 1 4.5,1.5 Z M 4.5,3 H 11.5 A 1.5,1.5 0 0 1 13,4.5 V 11.5 A 1.5,1.5 0 0 1 11.5,13 H 4.5 A 1.5,1.5 0 0 1 3,11.5 V 4.5 A 1.5,1.5 0 0 1 4.5,3 Z M 3.25,8 A 2.75,2.75 0 0 1 8.75,8 L 7.25,8 A 1.25,1.25 0 0 0 4.75,8 Z M 7.25,8 A 2.75,2.75 0 0 0 12.75,8 L 11.25,8 A 1.25,1.25 0 0 1 8.75,8 Z</x:String>

    <!--
        Holdover: §9.9's pause inside a clock face. This one is the reason the set was authored -
        the medallion had been borrowing a generic Warning glyph for a state that is specific, and
        "something is wrong" is not what holdover means. The oscillator is still disciplining; it is
        doing it from memory.
    -->
    <x:String x:Key="WzIconHoldover">F0 M 1.5,8 A 6.5,6.5 0 1 0 14.5,8 A 6.5,6.5 0 1 0 1.5,8 Z M 3,8 A 5,5 0 1 0 13,8 A 5,5 0 1 0 3,8 Z M 6.25,6.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 7.75,6.25 V 9.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 6.25,9.75 Z M 8.25,6.25 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 9.75,6.25 V 9.75 A 0.75,0.75 0 0 1 8.25,9.75 Z</x:String>

</ResourceDictionary>